[ti:Somewhere, Sometime (2026 Version)]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:My Anima]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:18.58]If I could find the words to say
[00:23.76]And strings to piece a tune
[00:26.34]I'd write a million songs to play
[00:32.89]To make your smile bloom
[00:36.28]If I could box the sun away
[00:41.40]And steal it from the sky
[00:46.09]I'd save it for a rainy day
[00:50.45]To raise your sunken eyes
[01:15.56]I don't care how long it takes
[01:21.34]Or how much breath I'll maybe waste
[01:25.14]I'll search this rock and many more
[01:30.19]We'll meet upon a distant star
[01:34.19]I've dreamt of you, ten thousand times
[01:38.92]But haven't seen your face
[01:43.44]And yet it feels, we've always touched
[01:47.39]Through oddities in time and space
[01:51.58]All I've ever really wanted
[01:56.53]Was you to help me build a rocket
[01:59.74]And blast away
[02:03.54]Far from this place, please
[02:08.26]Blast away with me, towards the stars
[02:16.22]Into the eye, of the man in the moon
[02:27.67]Wave goodbye, and close the capsule door
[02:34.91]We'll watch the world shrink away, as we depart
[03:02.31]If I'm with you I'm fairly certain
[03:07.42]Nothing out there would make me frightened
[03:12.01]I'd only need to hear your voice
[03:16.25]And all my doubts would be destroyed
[03:20.24]So if one day, our fuel runs out
[03:24.48]And we're barreling towards a black hole's mouth
[03:29.19]I'd want to hold your hands in mine
[03:32.18]And count the seconds passing by
[03:38.26]I'd be happy then and there
[03:42.16]Just grateful that I got to share
[03:45.88]A perfect moment, in a perfect life
[03:50.30]With you always by my side
[04:17.83]Somewhere, sometime
[04:22.48]Beyond the sun's shine
[04:26.32]Over the rainbow
[04:31.63]Under three moon's glow
[04:35.33]You're staring at the sky
[04:40.40]Waiting for my flashing lights
[04:44.16]To descend, from the stars
[04:48.78]And then at last, we're not apart
[05:10.12]Would I know the words to say
[05:13.60]Could I find the notes to play
[05:18.68]To ask you would you join my trek
[05:22.70]Throughout the universe and back
